{
  "schema_version": 5,
  "sha": "532d78658414d8f9aabce52cb64b982b3ec53388",
  "parent_shas": [
    "074019737caac1c6e6a457e3bed7e4a30e0a5877"
  ],
  "cutoff_date": "2025-06-02T02:03:38+02:00",
  "annotation": {
    "schema_version": 5,
    "type": "new architecture support",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "Gemma3's vision component previously contained load/unload stubs. This change supplies image preprocessing, a vision tower and projection into text-model embedding space.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_99741885323c4ebdad7d1f1e30f8f002"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "The implementation connects existing convolution, positional embedding, attention and MLP modules rather than adding a separate execution engine. Configuration parsing, module assembly and the image-shaped autosplit input are mutually supporting parts of that integration.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_99741885323c4ebdad7d1f1e30f8f002",
          "call_47a15fac148f483b8bb60649800b7506"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "Gemma3Config now unconditionally requires vision dimensions and preprocessor_config.json, including an asserted Gemma3ImageProcessor type. These requirements apply when constructing the conditional-generation configuration even if the caller selects its text component. The separate Gemma3TextConfig is not changed.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_99741885323c4ebdad7d1f1e30f8f002",
          "call_47a15fac148f483b8bb60649800b7506"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "The Gemma3 introduction entry was read: it establishes the earlier text implementation and explicitly unfinished vision component. The vision-helper entry was also read: it records that pixel rescaling and integration were previously caller responsibilities.",
        "basis": "ancestor",
        "evidence": [
          "call_f4784c8810c8487a90f74e65f70c94a2",
          "call_879c8faa36da47ab8288e80e37043eda"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Issue #7, \u201cquantizing model: undefined symbol: __cxa_call_terminate,\u201d reports a native-extension import failure and a reporter-provided environment workaround. Its relationship here is only an inferred shared model.py path, not evidence of a vision-model failure or a fix in this change.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_20d0986976fc477e95eab139a404f412",
          "call_99741885323c4ebdad7d1f1e30f8f002"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "No model loading, image-library operation, tensor operation or GPU inference was executed. The computation checks integer shape arithmetic only.",
      "Checkpoint configuration agreement does not establish numerical parity or weight-layout compatibility; tensor headers and preprocessor configuration files were not inspected.",
      "Pooling assumes a square patch grid and suitable divisibility by the requested token-grid side. Nonstandard configurations and rectangular preprocessing sizes were not validated.",
      "Whole-tree compatibility inspection was incomplete for configuration consumers and inherited module interfaces."
    ],
    "links": [
      "966762a32d1eb2c0aa5e01b02451676bca6ca7fd",
      "074019737caac1c6e6a457e3bed7e4a30e0a5877"
    ],
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "models",
        "title": "Gemma3 image-to-token embedding pipeline",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "Preprocessing converts transparency onto white through convert_to_rgb, resizes once, converts pixels to float32, applies the configured rescale factor, then channelwise (image \u2212 mean) / std. Only afterward does it transpose channels first and create a half-precision tensor with a leading batch dimension. Rescaling before normalization supplies the value-scale preparation the existing helper does not perform.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_99741885323c4ebdad7d1f1e30f8f002",
              "call_da03695ac8ca4ed2810c93286e0c5604"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Conv uses patch size as convolution stride and returns flattened spatial tokens. PosEmbedding adds consecutive learned position vectors from index zero. The tower then uses pre-attention and pre-MLP LayerNorm, attention without RoPE, and ordinary fc1/GELU/fc2 MLPs. The selected GELU implementation uses the tanh approximation; pad_to=1 preserves the checkpoint's unaligned intermediate width.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_99741885323c4ebdad7d1f1e30f8f002",
              "call_740f84e5344e4acb855b54ce06630df9",
              "call_2bb4a18850384696ae626220f6fd1c79",
              "call_59647c70cc01484681a0dc42da9baa29"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "get_image_embeddings invokes the inherited sequential forward with causal=False. Attention defaults to the no-cache FlashAttention path, which passes that flag to flash_attn_func. It does not select the cache-bearing decoder. The existing SDPA alternative rejects sliding windows and softcaps, neither of which this tower configures.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_99741885323c4ebdad7d1f1e30f8f002",
              "call_47a15fac148f483b8bb60649800b7506",
              "call_7d66692fb1e1466fa15bd7cfc2a11f3d"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "After post-LayerNorm, Gemma3MMPool reshapes tokens into a spatial grid and average-pools nonoverlapping neighborhoods. RMSNorm with constant_bias=1 follows, then a linear projection to text hidden width. The projector explicitly requests transposed_load=False. The pool has no weights and no loading work.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_99741885323c4ebdad7d1f1e30f8f002"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "All eleven inspected conditional-generation configurations specify the same vision geometry: width 1152, intermediate width 4304, 16 attention heads, 27 layers, image side 896, patch side 14 and 256 image tokens. This holds individually for google/gemma-3-4b-it, google/gemma-3-4b-pt, google/gemma-3-12b-it, google/gemma-3-12b-pt, google/gemma-3-27b-it and google/gemma-3-27b-pt. Their projector output widths are respectively 2560, 2560, 3840, 3840, 5376 and 5376.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_9a8fccb3b9df410587a75a024ccac693",
              "call_0a925d399669437ebdf7ccee7a27b52b",
              "call_8257be1a4dd5483bbb885ff0f891fea7",
              "call_a578415257334e0c8cf073d4f76a0ef7",
              "call_b60591316b8c49068f8ea9904459bc87",
              "call_cee7548a5ce74dbaa34b140326c9b994",
              "call_99741885323c4ebdad7d1f1e30f8f002"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The same vision dimensions hold individually for google/gemma-3-4b-it-qat-int4-unquantized, google/gemma-3-4b-it-qat-q4_0-unquantized, google/gemma-3-12b-it-qat-int4-unquantized, google/gemma-3-12b-it-qat-q4_0-unquantized and google/gemma-3-27b-it-qat-q4_0-unquantized; their text widths are 2560, 2560, 3840, 3840 and 5376. These five explicitly specify three channels, LayerNorm epsilon 1e-6 and tanh GELU, agreeing with the implementation's fixed choices. All eleven omit vision KV-head count and head dimension, so the adapter defaults them to 16 and 1152/16 rather than using text-attention dimensions.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_9835266bd9244ceba3ca4e5f8ada00bd",
              "call_0526c190d1ed48b587579fea857e1886",
              "call_1333953733be4139bdffdc1796912100",
              "call_2f2c2c46b68d48f7a616d6e621fda7d9",
              "call_be77a8a1c626457ba169df19a28a9952",
              "call_99741885323c4ebdad7d1f1e30f8f002"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A standard-library arithmetic transcription gives head dimension 72, a 64\u00d764 patch grid containing 4096 tokens, and a 4\u00d74 pooling kernel producing 16\u00d716 = 256 tokens. Adding the image boundary tokens gives a 258-token representation. It also shows that ordinary 128-alignment would round intermediate width 4304 to 4352, explaining the practical significance of pad_to=1.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_5501d8bd6a4a466c86f64ec0ec9879f9"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The final image vectors move to CPU and lose the singleton batch dimension. The method surrounds one -1 placeholder per vector with tokenizer IDs for <start_of_image> and <end_of_image>, then constructs MMEmbedding. That container replaces placeholders with allocated synthetic IDs and stores the original vectors and alias. The new method adds original size, preprocessed size and architecture metadata; no existing literal MMEmbedding constructor call was found in the parent tree.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_99741885323c4ebdad7d1f1e30f8f002",
              "call_b199b575b7f0416fa2160d86b76c5bdf",
              "call_8702d1966214415aa9413821acbdb980"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The autosplit override supplies a half-precision (1, channels, height, width) probe instead of integer token IDs. Model._load_autosplit consumes this hook before forwarding through modules, so this edit enables the convolution-first assembly to participate in the existing memory-probing loader.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_99741885323c4ebdad7d1f1e30f8f002",
              "call_47a15fac148f483b8bb60649800b7506"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "findings": [],
    "summary": "Implements Gemma3's vision component, from normalized images through pooled vision features to synthetic-token embeddings, while adding mandatory vision preprocessing configuration."
  },
